# SB Gunmetal.ask -- Ableton Live theme XML, converted by tools/themes/ask_to_theme.py
# SB_GUNMETAL_MOD: the pack's SB Gunmetal with four Live roles changed by --set
# and our two optional keys appended by hand (architect 2026-11-07..12):
#   WaveformColor 090A0C -> 151619: THE STEM-OVER-INK RULE, the ink lit above
#     the selection stem (ControlContrastFrame 0B0D11) by SB Bronze's step,
#     CIELAB L* 3.61, the hue kept by scaling linear RGB (session 98).
#   ControlForeground BEB3A5 -> B3B4BD, TextDisabled 7E7469 -> 737581: Live's
#     Cool Medium text pair in place of the pack's, which is Live's Warm
#     Medium pair (2026-11-12, session 113).
#   RangeDefault DFE2CF -> 535763: the playhead's head = the theme's own
#     BackgroundClip; its fill thereby equals the disabled chips', the
#     outlines and the lane telling them apart (2026-11-12, session 113, R2).
#   PlayheadLine=7E818A: the head 535763 moved 25 % toward white
#     (2026-11-12, session 113).
#   ControlContrastFrameDisabled=1E2026: 75 % of the way from
#     ControlContrastFrame 0B0D11 toward the marker lane's ground Desktop
#     24262D, 29.75 / 31.75 / 38 rounded half to even (2026-11-12, his pick
#     test7 over test6's 50 %).
# PlayheadLine and ControlContrastFrameDisabled are OUR OPTIONAL KEYS, not
# Live roles (src/gui/theme_roles.h's THE FORMAT): the converter writes Live
# roles only, so the last two lines were appended by hand after its output.
